Change-Id: orkosmpvsuxnxxqnytoovmxszwxtywnp
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:23:04 +0000

lab-process-mail drains the inbox once and exits, so new mail waits
until the operator runs it again by hand. lab-process-maild reruns it
every minute in the background, so the inbox stays answered without
anyone watching.

The operator only types start, stop, or status. daemon(8) does the
detaching, and run stays in the foreground for any other supervisor.

It is configured the way an rc(8) service is. The package installs
under a LOCALBASE, such as ~/local, but the log and pidfile belong to
the host, so each has its own setting in an rc.conf(5)-style file
under LOCALBASE/etc. Their defaults are /var/log and /var/run for root
and ~/log and ~/var/run for anyone else, so a user install works with
no conf at all.

Each pass starts from an empty environment plus what
lab_process_maild_env names, so how the daemon behaves does not depend
on which shell happened to start it. stop lets the pass in progress
finish, so a reply is never left half sent.

A failed run stops the daemon instead of retrying. A stuck message
stays oldest in the inbox, so a retry would spend an agent pass on it
every interval while the stuck notice has already gone out.

lab-process-maild(8) documents the commands and every setting.
